Glaze Ice
Glaze ice accretions occur at temperatures near freezing,
where the water droplets run back on the surface before freez
ing. While rime ice shapes are fairly streamlined, glaze ice ac
cretions usually present a drastic change in the airfoil shape.
This results in sometimes large regions of flow separation aft
of the ice horns. As a result of the separation, the airfoil ex
periences a severe drag rise, reduction in Qmax, and some
change in pitching moment. At the present time, no analytical
